                "senderName": "NWS Lake Charles LA",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 5 at 3:46PM CDT until September 5 at 5:45PM CDT by NWS Lake Charles LA",
                "description": "At 346 PM CDT, local law enforcement reported thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain in DeRidder. Up to 2 to 4 inches of rain have fallen.\nAdditional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible in the warned\narea. Flash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Law enforcement reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nDe Ridder, Rosepine and Tulla.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
